WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.074
Take a made-up shop.

2
00:00:04.074 --> 00:00:09.775
web calls checkout, checkout calls payments, and payments uses a Postgres database.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:17.452
At 10:02, the database connection pool inside payments fills up, and database calls start to wait.

4
00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:22.153
In your Part 12 stack, each symptom fires its own rule, within a minute.

5
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:23.565
Every alert is true.

6
00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:26.561
And none of them says which one caused the others.

7
00:00:26.561 --> 00:00:28.957
You dig through three tools to find out.

8
00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.460
Dynatrace starts with OneAgent, installed once per host.

9
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.692
It finds every process, and works out what it is.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.540
It loads a small code module into supported processes.

11
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.113
The module records each request as it passes through.

12
00:00:44.113 --> 00:00:45.731
Nobody changed the code.

13
00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:47.988
But how does it know who calls whom?

14
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.679
The module in the caller adds a trace header to each outgoing request.

15
00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:54.983
The module in the receiver reads it.

16
00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:57.287
So both ends of the call are linked.

17
00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.856
Smartscape records each link it sees.

18
00:00:59.856 --> 00:01:03.423
That is the live map of everything, and it draws itself.

19
00:01:03.633 --> 00:01:08.765
Every metric, log line and span carries the ID of the entity it came from.

20
00:01:08.765 --> 00:01:13.481
That shared ID is how the signals join, with no join logic from you.

21
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.099
Davis is the engine that watches all of this.

22
00:01:17.099 --> 00:01:22.896
First, it learns a baseline for each service: what normal looks like for it, at this time.

23
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.757
At 10:02, three services leave their baselines.

24
00:01:26.757 --> 00:01:29.791
Davis sees the same symptoms as events.

25
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.901
Then it walks.

26
00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:36.307
It starts at the affected entity, web, and follows the links to what web depends on.

27
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:39.760
At each one it asks: are you unhealthy too?

28
00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:40.661
checkout is.

29
00:01:40.661 --> 00:01:42.612
So Davis keeps going down.

30
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:44.680
payments is unhealthy too.

31
00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:48.515
The time in the traces piles up in its database calls.

32
00:01:48.515 --> 00:01:49.296
Keep going.

33
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.477
Postgres itself looks healthy.

34
00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:54.639
The waiting happens in the pool inside payments.

35
00:01:54.639 --> 00:01:56.155
So the trail ends here.

36
00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:59.515
Dynatrace calls this walk a fault-tree analysis.

37
00:01:59.515 --> 00:02:03.581
It ends at an unhealthy part whose own dependencies look fine.

38
00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:06.008
That is the most probable root cause.

39
00:02:06.233 --> 00:02:09.774
So Davis opens one problem, not four alerts.

40
00:02:09.774 --> 00:02:11.383
An ID, like P-12345.

41
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:13.234
The category, slowdown.

42
00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:18.143
payments as the root cause, and web and checkout as affected.

43
00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:22.805
Two graphs that spiked in the same minute are not linked by timing alone.

44
00:02:22.805 --> 00:02:25.420
The link comes from the map and the traces.

45
00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:29.202
Now remove OneAgent from payments, in your head.

46
00:02:29.202 --> 00:02:32.653
Nobody instruments it, so the map has no link into it.

47
00:02:32.867 --> 00:02:38.774
Davis would stop at checkout, because it cannot follow a call into something nobody instruments.

48
00:02:38.774 --> 00:02:41.605
A pipe without a sensor does not exist for it.

49
00:02:42.533 --> 00:02:44.372
OneAgent sees each process.

50
00:02:44.372 --> 00:02:47.299
Smartscape draws the map from what it sees.

51
00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:49.069
One ID joins every signal.

52
00:02:49.069 --> 00:02:53.291
And Davis walks that map, from the symptoms to one root cause.
